course: dictionary
lesson: 12806
title: Elimination: getting rid of what is wrong
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Elimination comes from the verb to eliminate, which means to remove or get rid of something completely. You will meet it in three main ways. In maths and puzzles, you use a process of elimination: you rule out wrong answers one by one until only the right one is left. «Sam crossed out 3, 7 and 9, so the answer must be 5.»
explain: In sport and games, elimination means being knocked out of a competition. «After losing both matches, our team faced elimination from the cup.» In a TV show, an elimination round sends one or more players home. In health and science, elimination means getting rid of something harmful or unwanted, such as «the elimination of waste from the body».
explain: To check the meaning, look at the clues around the word. In a puzzle, the words "wrong answers" and "one by one" tell you it is about ruling things out. In a competition, the words "knocked out" or "went home" tell you it is about losing your place. Then swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Elimination means removing or getting rid of something completely.
fact: A process of elimination means solving a problem by ruling out wrong answers one by one.
fact: In sport and shows, elimination means being knocked out of a competition.
fact: In science, the elimination of waste is how the body gets rid of what it does not need.
exercise: «Sam used elimination to solve the puzzle: he crossed out each wrong answer.» What did Sam do? | *Ruled out wrong answers one by one | Guessed at random | Added up all the numbers | Copied from a friend
exercise: «After losing both matches, our team faced elimination from the cup.» What does elimination mean here? | Winning a prize | Starting a new game | Practising for hours | *Being knocked out of the competition
exercise: «The doctor explained the elimination of waste from the body.» Which word is closest in meaning to elimination? | *Removal | Singing | Growing | Cooking
test: «The detective used a process of elimination and ruled out three suspects.» What does this show? | Arresting everybody at once | Keeping every suspect on the list | Asking the suspects to leave town | *Ruling out suspects one by one
test: «In the elimination round, the two weakest singers went home.» What is an elimination round? | A round with no rules | A round where everyone wins a prize | *A round where some players are knocked out | A holiday trip for the singers
exam: «The doctor explained the elimination of harmful germs from the body.» What does elimination mean here? | Making something louder | Growing something new | Cooking something slowly | *Getting rid of something completely
